"004:001 And king Solomon reigned over Israel.",
"004:002 And these are the princes which he had; Azarias son of Sadoc.",
"004:003 Eliaph, and Achia son of Seba, scribes; and Josaphat son of Achilud, recorder.",
"004:004 And Banaeas son of Jodae over the host; and Sadoc and Abiathar were priests.",
"004:005 And Ornia the son of Nathan was over the officers; and Zabuth son of Nathan was the king's friend.",
"004:006 And Achisar was steward, and Eliac the chief steward; and Eliab the son of Saph was over the family: and Adoniram the son of Audon over the tribute.",
"004:007 And Solomon had twelve officers over all Israel, to provide for the king and his household; each one's turn came to supply for a month in the year.",
"004:008 And these were their names: Been the son of Or in the mount of Ephraim, one.",
"004:009 The son of Dacar, in Makes, and in Salabin, and Baethsamys, and Elon as far as Bethanan, one.",
"004:010 The son of Esdi in Araboth; his was Socho, and all the land of Opher.",
"004:011 All Nephthador belonged to the son of Aminadab, Tephath daughter of Solomon was his wife, one.",
"004:012 Bana son of Achiluth had Ithaanach, and Mageddo, and his was the whole house of San which was by Sesathan below Esrae, and from Bethsan as far as Sabelmaula, as far as Maeber Lucam, one.",
"004:013 The son of Naber in Raboth Galaad, to him fell the lot of Ergab in Basan, sixty great cities with walls, and brazen bars, one.",
"004:014 Achinadab son of Saddo, had Maanaim.",
"004:015 Achimaas was in Nephthalim, and he took Basemmath daughter of Solomon to wife, one.",
"004:016 Baana son of Chusi, in Aser and in Baaloth, one,",
"004:017 Josaphat son of Phuasud was in Issachar.",
"004:018 Semei son of Ela, in Benjamin.",
"004:019 Gaber son of Adai in the land of Gad, the land of Seon king of Esebon, and of Og king of Basan, and one officer in the land of Juda.",
"004:020 3:1n  And king Solomon was very prudent and wise:  and Juda and Israel were very many, as the sand which is by the sea for multitude, eating, and drinking, and rejoicing:",
"004:021 3:1o  and Solomon was chief in all the kingdoms, and they brought gifts, and served Solomon all the days of his life:",
"004:022 And these were the requisite supplies for Solomon: in one day thirty measures of fine flour, and sixty measures of fine pounded meal,",
"004:023 and ten choice calves, and twenty pastured oxen, and one hundred sheep, besides stags, and choice fatted does.",
"004:024 For he had dominion on this side the river, and he was at peace on all sides round about.",
"004:025 3:1r  For he ruled in all the country on this side the river, from Raphi to Gaza, over all the kings on this side the river: and he was at peace on all sides round about; and Juda and Israel lived safely, every one under his vine and under his fig tree, eating and drinand feasting, from Dan even to Bersabee, all the days of Solomon.",
"004:026 3:1t  And Solomon had forty thousand brood mares for his chariots, and twelve thousand horses.",
"004:027 4:20 And thus the officers provided king Solomon: and they execute every one in his month all the orders for the table of the king, they omit nothing.",
"004:028 4:21 And they carried the barley and the straw for the horses and the chariots to the place where the king might be, each according to his charge.",
"004:029 And the Lord gave understanding to Solomon, and very much wisdom, and enlargement of heart, as the sand on the seashore.",
"004:030 And Solomon abounded greatly beyond the wisdom of all the ancients, and beyond all the wise men of Egypt.",
"004:031 And he was wiser than all other men: and he was wiser than Gaethan the Zarite, and than Aenan, and than Chalcad and Darala the son of Mal.",
"004:032 And Solomon spoke three thousand proverbs, and his songs were five thousand.",
"004:033 And he spoke of trees, from the cedar in Libanus even to the hyssop which comes out through the wall: he spoke also of cattle, and of birds, and of reptiles, and of fishes.",
"004:034 And all the nations came to hear the wisdom of Solomon, and ambassadors from all the kings of the earth, as many as heard of his wisdom. And Solomon took to himself the daughter of Pharao to wife, and brought her into the city of David until he had finished the house of the Lord, and his own house, and the wall of Jerusalem. Then went up Pharao the king of Egypt, and took Gazer, and burnt it and the Chananite dwelling in Mergab; and Pharao gave them as a dowry to his daughter the wife of Solomon: and Solomon rebuilt Gazer."
