"007:001 7:51b  And Solomon built a house for himself in thirteen years.",
"007:002 7:51c  And he built the house with the wood of Libanus; its length was one hundred cubits, and its breadth was fifty cubits, and its height was of thirty cubits, and it was made with three rows of cedar pillars, and the pillars had side-pieces of cedar.",
"007:003 7:51d  And he formed the house with chambers above on the sides of the pillars,  and the number of the pillars was each row forty and five,",
"007:004 7:51e  and there were three chambers,",
"007:005 7:51f  And all the doors and spaces formed like chambers were square, and from door to door was a correspondence in three rows.",
"007:006 7:51g  And he made the porch of the pillars, they were fifty cubits long and fifty broad, the porch joining them in front; and the other pillars and the thick beam were in front of the house by the porches.",
"007:007 7:51h  And there was the Porch of seats where he would judge, the porch of judgement.",
"007:008 7:51i  And their house where he would dwell, had one court communicating with these according to this work; and he built the house for the daughter of Pharao whom Solomon had taken, according to this porch.",
"007:009 7:51j  All these were of costly stones,  sculptured at intervals within even from the foundation even to the top,  and outward to the great court,",
"007:010 7:51k  founded with large costly stones,  stones of ten cubits and eight cubits long,",
"007:011 7:51l  And above with costly stones, according to the measure of hewn stones, and with cedars.",
"007:012 7:51m  There were three rows of hewn stones round about the great hall, and a row of sculptured cedar: and Solomon finished all his house.",
"007:013 And king Solomon sent, and took Chiram out of Tyre,",
"007:014 the son of a widow woman; and he was of the tribe of Nephthalim, and his father was a Tyrian; a worker in brass, and accomplished in are and skill and knowledge to work every work in brass: and he was brought in to king Solomon, and he wrought all the works.",
"007:015 And he cast the two pillars for the porch of the house: eighteen cubits was the height of each pillar, and a circumference of fourteen cubits encompassed it, even the thickness of the pillar: the flutings were four fingers wide, and thus was the other pillar formed.",
"007:016 And he made two molten capitals to put on the heads of the pillars: five cubits was the height of one chapiter, and five cubits was the height of the other chapiter.",
"007:017 And he made two ornaments of network to cover the capitals of the pillars; even a net for one chapiter, and a net for the other chapiter.",
"007:018 7:18a And hanging work, two rows of brazen pomegranates, formed with network, hanging work, row upon row: and thus he framed the ornaments for the second chapiter.",
"007:019 And on the heads of the pillars he made lily-work against the porch, of four cubits,",
"007:020 and a chamber over both the pillars, and above the sides an addition equal to the chamber in width.",
"007:021 7:18b  And he set up the pillars of the porch of the temple: and he set up the one pillar, and called its name Jachum: and he set up the second pillar, and called its name Boloz.",
"007:022 OMITTED TEXT",
