"021:001 20:1 And Nabuthai the Jezraelite had a vineyard, near the threshing floor of Achaab king of Samaria.",
"021:002 20:2 And Achaab spoke to Nabuthai, saying, Give me your vineyard, and I will have it for a garden of herbs, for it is near my house: and I will give you another vineyard better than it; or if it please you, I will give you money, the price of this your vineyard, and I will have it for a garden of herbs.",
"021:003 20:3 And Nabuthai said to Achaab, My God forbid me that I should give you the inheritance of my fathers.",
"021:004 20:4 And the spirit of Achaab was troubled, and he lay down upon his bed, and covered his face, and ate no bread.",
"021:005 20:5 And Jezabel his wife went in to him, and spoke to him, saying, Why is your spirit troubled, and why do you eat no bread?",
"021:006 20:6 And he said to her, Because I spoke to Nabuthai the Jezraelite, saying, Give me your vineyard for money; or if you will, I will give you another vineyard for it: and he said, I will not give you the inheritance of my fathers.",
"021:007 20:7 And Jezabel his wife said to him, Do you now thus act the king over Israel? arise, and eat bread, and be your own master, and I will give you the vineyard of Nabuthai the Jezraelite.",
"021:008 20:8 And she wrote a letter in the name of Achaab, and sealed it with his seal, and sent the letter to the elders, and to the freemen who lived with Nabuthai.",
"021:009 20:9 And it was written in the letters, saying, Keep a fast, and set Naboth in a chief place amongst the people.",
"021:010 20:10 And set two men, sons of transgressors, before him, and let them testify against him, saying, He blessed God and the king: and let them lead him forth, and stone him, and let them die.",
"021:011 20:11 And the men of his city, the elders, and the nobles who lived in his city, did as Jezabel sent to them, and as it had been written in the letters which she sent to them.",
"021:012 20:12 And they proclaimed a fast, and set Nebuthai in a chief place amongst the people.",
"021:013 20:13 And two men, sons of transgressors, came in, and sat opposite him, and bore witness against him, saying, You have blessed God and the king. And they led him forth out of the city, and stoned him with stones, and he died.",
"021:014 20:14 And they sent to Jezabel, saying, Nabuthai is stoned, and is dead.",
"021:015 20:15 And it came to pass, when Jezabel heard it, that she said to Achaab, Arise, take possession of the vineyard of Nabuthai the Jezraelite, who would not sell it to you: for Nebuthai is not alive, for he is dead.",
"021:016 20:16 And it came to pass, when Achaab heard that Nabuthai the Jezraelite was dead, that he tore his garments, and put on sackcloth. And it came to pass afterward, that Achaab arose and went down to the vineyard of Nabuthai the Jezraelite, to take possession of it.",
"021:017 20:17 And the Lord spoke to Eliu the Thesbite, saying,",
"021:018 20:18 Arise, and go down to meet Achaab king of Israel, who is in Samaria, for he is in the vineyard of Nabuthai, for he has gone down there to take possession of it.",
"021:019 20:19 And you shall speak to him, saying, Thus says the Lord, Forasmuch as you have slain and taken possession, therefore thus says the Lord, In every place where the swine and the dogs have licked the blood of Nabuthai, there shall the dogs lick your blood; and the harlots shall wash themselves in your blood.",
"021:020 20:20 And Achaab said to Eliu, Have you found me, my enemy? and he said, I have found you: because you have wickedly sold yourself to work evil in the sight of the Lord, to provoke him to anger;",
"021:021 20:21 behold, I bring evil upon you: and I will kindle a fire after you, and I will utterly destroy every male of Achaab, and him that is shut up and him that is left in Israel.",
"021:022 20:22 And I will make your house as the house of Jeroboam the son of Nabat, and as the house of Baasa son of Achia, because of the provocations wherewith you have provoked me, and caused Israel to sin.",
"021:023 20:23 And the Lord spoke of Jezabel, saying, The dogs shall devour her within the fortification of Jezrael.",
"021:024 20:24 Him that is dead of Achaab in the city shall the dogs eat, and him that is dead of him in the field shall the birds of the sky eat.",
"021:025 20:25 But Achaab did wickedly, in that he sold himself to do that which was evil in the sight of the Lord, as his wife Jezabel led him astray.",
"021:026 20:26 And he did very abominably in following after the abominations, according to all that the Amorite did, whom the Lord utterly destroyed from before the children of Israel.",
"021:027 20:27 And because of the word, Achaab was pierced with sorrow before the Lord, and he both went weeping, and tore his garment, and girded sackcloth upon his body, and fasted; he put on sackcloth also in the day that he struck Nabuthai the Jezraelite, and went his way.",
"021:028 20:28 And the word of the Lord came by the hand of his servant Eliu concerning Achaab, and the Lord said,",
"021:029 20:29 Have you seen how Achaab has been pricked to the heart before me? I will not bring on the evil in his days, but in his son's days will I bring on the evil."
